%I A302613 #18 Nov 14 2026 09:23:48
%S A302613 2,2,2,4,8,12,16,32,64
%N A302613 Total domination number of the n-folded cube graph.
%C A302613 107 <= a(11) <= 120; 180 <= a(12) <= 240; 342 <= a(13) <= 380; 598 <= a(14) <= 760; 1172 <= a(15) <= 1408. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Nov 14 2026
%H A302613 J. Azarija, M. A. Henning and S. Klavzar, <a href="https://users.fmf.uni-lj.si/klavzar/preprints/Electronic_JC_Azarija_Henning_Klavzar_2017.pdf">(Total) Domination in Prisms</a>, Electron. J. Combin. 24(1) (2017), P1.19.
%H A302613 G. Keri, <a href="https://old.sztaki.hu/~keri/codes/2_tables.pdf">Bounds on K(n, R), R = 1, 2, 3</a>.
%H A302613 Y. S. Kwon and J. Lee, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dam.2013.09.020">Perfect domination sets in Cayley graphs</a>, Discrete Appl. Math. 162 (2014), 259-263.
%H A302613 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/FoldedCubeGraph.html">Folded Cube Graph</a>.
%H A302613 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HypercubeGraph.html">Hypercube Graph</a>.
%H A302613 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TotalDominationNumber.html">Total Domination Number</a>.
%F A302613 From _Eric W. Weisstein_, Nov 14 2026: (Start)
%F A302613 Let gamma(G) denote the domination number of G, Q_n the n-dimensional hypercube graph, and F_n the n-folded cube graph.
%F A302613 For odd n >= 3, a(n) = gamma(Q_(n-1)).
%F A302613 For even n >= 4, a(n) = 2*gamma(F_(n-1)).
%F A302613 a(2^r) = 2^(2^r-r-1) for r >= 2.
%F A302613 a(2^r+1) = 2^(2^r-r) for r >= 1.
%F A302613 For even n >= 4, gamma(Q_(n-1)) <= a(n) <= 2*gamma(Q_(n-2)).
%F A302613 (End)
%K A302613 nonn,more,changed
%O A302613 2,1
%A A302613 _Eric W. Weisstein_, Apr 10 2018
%E A302613 a(10) from _Eric W. Weisstein_, Aug 27 2021
